title: $:/plugins/tiddlywiki/hard-line-breaks/readme

This plugin adds the `ssnl` wikitext rule: two spaces, or two spaces and a backslash, before the line end make a hard line break anywhere, list items and headings included, as in CommonMark. A blank line still separates paragraphs.

```
* Roses are red
Violets are blue
* Sugar is sweet  \
And so are you
```

`\rules except ssnl` switches the rule off. An editor that writes wikitext should use the backslash form, which survives tools that trim trailing whitespace. With the wikitext-serialize plugin installed, a break serializes back to the same text.
